# What the production image must NOT contain.
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything missing here ends up on the server —
# including secrets. Deny broadly; the server only needs its own JS + public/.

# Secrets and local state — never in an image
.env
.env.*
certs
data
ssh-key-*
*.pem
*.key

# VCS / tooling / local notes
.git
.github
.githooks
.claude
CLAUDE.md
.vscode

# Dependencies are installed inside the image, not copied in
node_modules

# Client shells: built and shipped as installers, not served by the app container
android
desktop
build
dist
*.apk
*.AppImage
*.exe
*.dmg

# Dev-only material — references, design handoffs, scratch work
dev
docs
scripts
lighthouserc.json

# Docs and compose files the runtime never reads
README.md
RELEASE.md
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
Dockerfile
Caddyfile

# Noise
*.log
.DS_Store
.flatpak-builder
